ith the scenario's values.\n- **Per scenario:**\n  - **logo-leads-home** (the main scenario): a Playwright browser test opens the \"Domain-Driven Design\" product page, checks the logo reads \"domaincentric.commerce\", clicks it, and asserts the path `/` and the home page heading.\n  - **The other four:** integration tests against the running app. They check the \"Home\" and \"Products\" links in the navigation, the footer's exact wording, the \"Event Log\" link to `/backoffice/events`, and that the home page's header and footer match the catalogue page's.\n- **Review perspectives:** I did not run the ddd, hexagonal, clean-code or dca reviews, since no production code changed. `dca-knowledge` is named in the profile, but no architecture question came up, so I didn't consult it.\n- **Breaks:** `tests.md` reports a break for each scenario under `tasks/CAT-05/breaks/` that turns its test red. That comes from the test stage's notes; I did not re-run them.\n- **Dropped, not blocking:** two of the integration tests take the page's first `<nav>` rather than the one inside the header. That is correct today, because the header's nav is the first one on every page. Limiting them to the header, as the fifth test does, would make them sturdier if a page ever adds a nav above it.","ttft_ms":3173,"type":"result","duration_ms":51605,"uuid":"cc76d7c1-329c-4fc4-ae21-0314abb56452","ttft_stream_ms":1936,"time_to_request_ms":58,"first_content_frame_ms":1936,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
